--TEST--
An array-element write whose root is only a temporary is refused, whichever write spelling and whichever root — `rule:types/arrays` and § 7 row 15
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/arrays` separates the array before an element is written, and
// `nvs_ir::lower::Lowering::write_back_array` has to put the separated copy
// back into whatever held it — a local, a property, or a static property. A
// root that is none of those holds it nowhere, so the write would be
// discarded: PHP 8.5 accepts every line below and drops it silently, which is
// `rule:types/an-element-write-needs-storage-to-write-back-into`'s divergence and `E0700` here. What this pins is that
// the four write spellings *agree* — `=`, `⊕=`, `$x++` and `--$x` all reach
// the rule through `nvs_types::expr::assign`'s one `check_write_target` — and
// that the root's own shape does not matter, only that it is not a place.
class Holder {
    public array<string> $rows;

    public function constructor() {
        array<string> $seed = ["a" => "x"];
        $this->rows = $seed;
    }

    public function rows(): array<string> {
        return $this->rows;
    }
}

Holder $h = new Holder();
array<string> $left = ["0" => "l"];
array<string> $right = ["0" => "r"];
bool $pick = true;

$h->rows()["a"] = "y";
$h->rows()["a"] .= "z";
$h->rows()["a"]++;
--$h->rows()["a"];
["q"]["0"] = "z";
($pick ? $left : $right)["0"] = "z";
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0700]: an array element cannot be written through a temporary
   --> case.nvs:29:1
